    "Medicaid",
    "Founded in 1984 as a single nonprofit Medicaid health plan in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, Centene Corporation has grown into the largest Medicaid managed care organization in the United States. Today, it serves approximately 12.1 million Medicaid members across 30 states.",
    "Centene is a national leader in Medicaid innovation and access. Our Medicaid programs are designed to meet the diverse needs of individuals and families.",
    "Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF)",
    "Medicaid Expansion",
    "Aged, Blind, Disabled (ABD)",
    "Children’s Health Insurance Program (CHIP)",
    "Long-Term Services and Supports (LTSS)",
    "Foster Care",
    "Dual Eligible Special Needs Plan (D-SNP)",
    "Other state-based programs",
    "Centene provides access to affordable, quality-focused healthcare not only to Medicaid members, but also to Medicare members through WellcareExternal Link, and to individuals and families served by the Health Insurance Marketplace through Ambetter HealthExternal Link. Wellcare offers a variety of Medicare options – including Medicare Advantage and Prescription Drug Plans – that go beyond Original Medicare (Parts A and B) to provide affordable, comprehensive coverage. Ambetter Health provides comprehensive coverage, including preventive and wellness services, maternity and newborn care, pediatric services, mental health and substance misuse treatment, prescription drug coverage, and more.",
